  "extra_findings": [
    "F3: the listing and search showed every client's tickets (index.php:72-73, lib.php:78-93). The delivery filters by usuario_id for non-technicians through listarChamadosVisiveis, which enforces the manifest's visibility rule. It is more than 10 lines from index.php:53, so it is not SEC-017.",
    "F4: index.php?export=csv gave any session the whole table (index.php:44-46). The web export is now filtered to the client's own tickets, while technicians and sessionless exportarCsv() callers still get every ticket (enforcement, not COMP-003). It describes the export route, not the ?ver= IDOR that F2 already covers.",
    "F7 items 1-2: the on-disk EXPORT_DIR/chamados.csv left the whole table under /var/www/painel/tmp (public only if the vhost serves it), and its fixed name raced between concurrent exports. Removed by streaming to php://output. Bundled in F7, which maps to BUG-004.",
    "F9 cookie part: the session cookie had no HttpOnly/SameSite. session_set_cookie_params was added. Bundled in F9, which maps to SEC-013.",
    "F12: mediaResposta fetched every answered row to sum it in PHP. Replaced by SUM()/COUNT(), with the division kept in PHP (AVG avoided to keep the value).",
    "F14: array-shaped login[] and busca[] parameters reach string-typed functions and raise an uncaught TypeError. is_string() guards were added.",
    "F16: formatarStatus maps any unknown status to 'Resolvido'. This is a contracted fallback and it was kept (rule 14).",
    "F17 items 1-3: rotuloPrioridade's labels for priority 4 without a response, priority 4 within SLA and priority 1 are called a possible rule bug. This is contracted behaviour and it was kept (rule 14). Bundled in F17, which maps to CLN-007.",
    "F18: the login form has no brute-force limit. Not fixed.",
    "Decisoes 10: no CSRF token on the login POST (SEC-005), no logout and no security headers. Recommended, not changed."
  ],
